      {
        "body": "Fresh departure closes at least max(one sigma, four ticks) from VWAP. Episodes mature after thirty minutes; checkpoint clock minute is divisible by ten and a full thirty-minute path must remain. A contact is future range intersection with checkpoint-frozen VWAP ±one tick; checkpoints already inside the zone are null. B freezes both barriers at the checkpoint and their unequal distances make fifty percent an inappropriate baseline. C requires a qualifying session-VWAP failure between mature day/session destinations, separated by at least eight ticks and a quarter day sigma, with thirty-minute lockout. Table outcomes use eligible checkpoint/event denominators, not independent trades. Saved 95% intervals use shared ISO-week clusters. Context-only models use frozen development cells and support fallbacks; negative relative Brier change means lower prediction error.",
        "id": "methods",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Definitions and methods"
      },
      {
        "body": "Previously viewed all-history evidence is exploratory. Episodes, repeated checkpoints and two-/five-minute sensitivities are dependent. OHLC cannot order two destinations touched in one candle; ambiguous is retained. Conditional probabilities and small model improvements do not prove causality, fills, net profitability or a pristine holdout.",
        "id": "limitations",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Limitations and uncertainty"
      },
      {
        "body": "Study 11_vwap_conditional_probabilities; source run 20260924T155331Z_vwap11. Registered reference: Explicit registered reference; retain its executed scope and saved qualifications.\n\nPresentation revision 20261006T230936Z_web11, web-study-report-1.0. Saved numerical tables are the authority; only selected rows and columns are presented. No new statistics or research execution. The publication record identifies this JSON and its selected assets.",
